# CLAUDE.md transport plan (§2, §5)
# Anchored (/results/, not results/): a bare `results/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, which was silently also catching
# layernorm_study/results/ - confirmed directly (2026-08-27, round 1) that
# this made a nested .gitignore's negation impossible to override (git's
# directory-exclusion short-circuit never descends into an already-
# excluded directory). Anchoring restricts this rule to the repo-root
# results/ dir only, which is the only thing it was ever meant to cover -
# behavior for that directory is unchanged either way.
/results/
wandb/
venv/
*.msgpack
!tests/fixtures/*.msgpack
!docs/nu_gap_export/ckpt/*.msgpack
!docs/b320/ckpt/*.msgpack

# raw per-(variant,case,seed) nu-gap export artifacts (large, intermediate -
# the analysis-ready output is docs/nu_gap_export_summary.csv, which IS
# tracked). Also the orchestrator's own operational log/status files.
#
# EXCEPTION (2026-08-19, TASK D): ckpt/ and dither_cured/ are the actual
# checkpoints for M3/M0_S4/M6/dither-cured models - small (~5MB combined,
# not the multi-MB-per-file Abar/Bbar npz exports this rule was written
# for) and load-bearing for reproducibility, so they are tracked despite
# living under this otherwise-ignored directory.
docs/nu_gap_export/*
!docs/nu_gap_export/ckpt/
!docs/nu_gap_export/dither_cured/
docs/n1000_case3/
docs/lqr_cache/

# TASK 4 (2026-08-25): B=320 identification. The per-checkpoint A/B/C
# npz exports (docs/b320/*.npz, 8.2MB each - the same size class as
# docs/nu_gap_export/'s large Abar/Bbar exports) are regeneratable from
# the small msgpack checkpoints (docs/b320/ckpt/) via
# tools/identify_b320.py's augmented_operator() - not committed. The
# checkpoints and analysis-ready CSVs (docs/b320/*.csv) ARE tracked.
docs/b320/*.npz
docs/dimension_sweep/
docs/stability_constrained/
docs/linear_ssm_baseline/
launch/colab/*.log
launch/colab/*_status.json

# TACC: local user config (host/path/partition only, but still not shared -
# tacc.env.example is the tracked template) + raw Slurm stdout/stderr, which
# job.slurm writes into the repo checkout itself on TACC.
launch/tacc/tacc.env
slurm-*.out
slurm-*.err

# local staging for `kaggle kernels output -p ./out` (§4) and any one-off
# comparison pulls (e.g. ./out-cpu/)
/out*/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/

.env
